/* Equilibrium of N SDPD particles at fixed total energy E0 and zero
total momentum. The stationary density of GENERIC is exp(S_tot/kB) in
(x, v, S); with X = exp(S), changing S_i to the internal energy E_i
gives a weight w(E_i) dE_i. The kinetic energy K has f = n (N - 1)
quadratic degrees of freedom, so K/E0 and every E_i/E0 are Dirichlet
distributed. */

assume(kB > 0, d > 0, En > 0, N > 1, E0 > 0)$
eos[2]: d*X$
eos[3]: 3/2*d^(2/3)*X^(2/3)$
for n: 2 thru 3 do block([S_E, w, c, f, a, b, K, U, ratio, al, var, varK, spread],
  S_E: log(rhs(first(solve(eos[n] = En, X)))),
  w: radcan(exp(S_E/kB)*diff(S_E, En)),
  c: ratsimp(En*diff(log(w), En) + 1)*kB,
  f: n*(N - 1),
  a: f/2,
  b: N*c/kB,
  K: E0*a/(a + b),
  U: E0*b/(a + b),
  ratio: ratsimp((2*K/(n*N))/(kB*U/(c*N))),
  al: c/kB,
  var: ratsimp((a + b - al)/(al*(a + b + 1))),
  varK: ratsimp(b/(a*(a + b + 1))),
  spread: ratsimp((N - 1)/(N*al + 1)),
  print(n, "D: w(E) =", w, ", C =", c, ", <m v_a^2>/<kB T> =", ratio,
    ", <dT^2>/<T>^2 =", var, "->", limit(var, N, inf),
    ", var(K)/<K>^2 =", varK, ", snapshot spread of T =", spread))$
